Outputs one of the game's combat status icons: buffs, debuffs, crowd control, and special and guide icons. The stylesheet draws their frames, which stay sharp at any size, around symbols from [[:File:Combat_Icon_Atlas.webp]].
==Usage==
<code><nowiki>{{CombatIcon|Name[|text=Text][|title=Tooltip][|link=Page][|size=24]}}</nowiki></code>
==Options==
*<code>Name</code>: the icon's name, which is its file name in the game without ''Combat_Icon_'' and ''.png'', such as <code>Buff_ATK</code>. Spaces can stand for underscores, as in file names. [[#Icons|The icons]] are listed below; a name that isn't one of them shows an empty frame. Without a name, only the text is shown
*<code>text</code>: text after the icon, such as the effect's name
*<code>title</code>: tooltip, which screen readers read too. Without one, the tooltip is the icon's name; an icon with text has none, and screen readers read the text
*<code>link</code>: page that the icon and its text link to
*<code>size</code>: height of the icon, in pixels or any CSS length such as <code>2em</code>; the width is automatic. To size all icons in a table or block at once, set <code>--combat-icon-size</code> in its style, such as <code><nowiki>style="--combat-icon-size:32px"</nowiki></code>
==Examples==
<syntaxhighlight lang="wikitext" copy>
{{CombatIcon|Buff_ATK}} {{CombatIcon|Debuff_DEF}} {{CombatIcon|CC_Stunned}} {{CombatIcon|Special_Fury}} {{CombatIcon|Guide_Question}}
</syntaxhighlight>
{{CombatIcon|Buff_ATK}} {{CombatIcon|Debuff_DEF}} {{CombatIcon|CC_Stunned}} {{CombatIcon|Special_Fury}} {{CombatIcon|Guide_Question}}

With text:
<syntaxhighlight lang="wikitext" copy>
Inflicts {{CombatIcon|CC_Stunned|text=Stun}} for 2 seconds and grants all allies {{CombatIcon|Buff_ATK|text=Attack Increase}}.
</syntaxhighlight>
Inflicts {{CombatIcon|CC_Stunned|text=Stun}} for 2 seconds and grants all allies {{CombatIcon|Buff_ATK|text=Attack Increase}}.

In a narrow column the text wraps, and the icon stays with its first word:
<syntaxhighlight lang="wikitext" copy>
<div style="width:11em; padding:4px 8px; border:1px solid #a2a9b1">Grants {{CombatIcon|Buff_TacticalShieldHealByHit_Damaged|text=Tactical Shield Recovery When Hit}} and inflicts {{CombatIcon|Debuff_ReduceWeakDamagedRate|text=Effective Damage Taken Increase}}.</div>
</syntaxhighlight>
<div style="width:11em; padding:4px 8px; border:1px solid #a2a9b1">Grants {{CombatIcon|Buff_TacticalShieldHealByHit_Damaged|text=Tactical Shield Recovery When Hit}} and inflicts {{CombatIcon|Debuff_ReduceWeakDamagedRate|text=Effective Damage Taken Increase}}.</div>

With a tooltip, and with a link:
<syntaxhighlight lang="wikitext" copy>
{{CombatIcon|Debuff_Burn|title=Burn}} {{CombatIcon|CC_Stunned|text=Stun|link=Category:Characters with stun skills}}
</syntaxhighlight>
{{CombatIcon|Debuff_Burn|title=Burn}} {{CombatIcon|CC_Stunned|text=Stun|link=Category:Characters with stun skills}}

Sizes, from the game's own 54px down, and at the default size in larger text:
<syntaxhighlight lang="wikitext" copy>
{{CombatIcon|Buff_Shield|size=54}} {{CombatIcon|Buff_Shield|size=32}} {{CombatIcon|Buff_Shield|size=24}} {{CombatIcon|Buff_Shield|size=16}} <span style="font-size:150%">{{CombatIcon|Buff_Shield|text=Shield}}</span>
</syntaxhighlight>
{{CombatIcon|Buff_Shield|size=54}} {{CombatIcon|Buff_Shield|size=32}} {{CombatIcon|Buff_Shield|size=24}} {{CombatIcon|Buff_Shield|size=16}} <span style="font-size:150%">{{CombatIcon|Buff_Shield|text=Shield}}</span>
